<question no="16269" partialPoint="true" point="100" skillType="4" type="matching">
	<title><![CDATA[Vocabulary]]></title>
	<direction><![CDATA[パッセージ中の空所を最も適当と思われる語句で埋めなさい。（空所をクリックまたはタップし、表示される語句の中から答えを選んでください。）]]></direction>
	<questionText><![CDATA[Typically, places of this [nature] in France [tended to] be rather formal and geometric, but Baron Haussman used the layout of Hyde Park in London to buck the [trend]. What he [ended up with] is a place where it is easy to [get lost]. However, by finding one of the [numerous] narrow paths that have been made by people taking a short-cut and following it, getting yourself out of trouble, [except] at night, is [relatively] easy.]]></questionText>

	<description><![CDATA[1. 解答：nature<br><br>X of this nature：<br>この性格/特徴をもつ X<br><br><br>2. 解答：tended to<br><br>tend to-不定詞：<br>～しがちである/～する傾向がある (= be likely/prone/apt/inclined to-不定詞)<br><br><br>3. 解答：trend<br><br>buck the trend：<br>その傾向に強く抵抗/対抗する（buck はここでは「～に強く抵抗/対抗する」の意味）<br><br>trend：<br>流行、傾向<br><br><br>4. 解答：ended up with<br><br>end up with~：<br>結果的に～になる/最終的に～で終わる/～という結末を迎える<br><br><br>5. 解答：get lost<br><br>get lost：<br>道に迷う (= lose one's way)（ただ「失せる」の意味もある）<br><br><br>6. 解答：numerous<br><br>numerous：<br>多数の、幾多の<br><br><br>7. 解答：except<br><br>except：<br>～以外は<br><br><br>8. 解答：relatively<br><br>relatively：<br>比較的]]></description>

</question>

